{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0151fmrh9wjmq9DatuDqwRVZ","type":"tool_result","content":"  microtags/htm (browser)\n  Size limit: 4.65 kB\n  Size:       4.61 kB with all dependencies, minified and brotlied\n  \nADR-007-client-templater.md\n\nComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\nused, and nothing where it is not.\n\nTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\ncomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\na host's markup.\n\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n\nThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\nhydration example uses it.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5a9ad4d-6356-4fe5-8bf2-17f416a3903b","uuid":"b4c78c19-18a8-41cc-9bc2-e2b082f5d945","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:01:42.120Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  microtags/htm (browser)\n  Size limit: 4.65 kB\n  Size:       4.61 kB with all dependencies, minified and brotlied\n  \nADR-007-client-templater.md\n\nComment markers add a few bytes to server output where reactivity is\nused, and nothing where it is not.\n\nTreating hosts as opaque keeps reconciliation simple and leaves a\ncomponent's internals to its own setup, but a region cannot patch inside\na host's markup.\n\n## Consequences\n\nADR-004 is relaxed for the templater subpath only. Its size-limit entry\nis raised to the measured result, and the browser build gets its own\nentry so growth stays visible. The core entry stays budgeted as before.\n\nADR-005 still holds: render links are stripped by default. A component\ncreated in the browser, for example as a list item, must be kept with\n`client: true` or the keep list.\n\nAfter a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's attribute no\nlonger tracks the current value. Tests and docs must read the property,\nnot the attribute.\n\nThe package gains a fourth browser build script and a `browser`\ncondition on the `./htm` export. Bundler aliases that point\n`microtags/htm` at source must make the same split.\n\nThis ADR supersedes no earlier decision. ADR-008 records how the\nhydration example uses it.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-07-markup-brand-symbol/.size-limit.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":6,"newStart":13,"newLines":6,"lines":["     {","         name: 'microtags/htm (browser)',","         path: 'dist/htm.browser.min.js',","-        limit: '4.6 kB',","+        limit: '4.65 kB',","     },"," ]"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-07-markup-brand-symbol/src/htm.browser.ts","hunks":[{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":7,"newStart":63,"newLines":7,"lines":[" }"," "," function _isMarkup (c:unknown):c is Markup {","-    return (c as Record<symbol, unknown> | null)?.[_M] === true","+    return c != null && (c as Record<symbol, unknown>)[_M] === true"," }"," "," function _isMicrotag (t:unknown):t is Comp {"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-07-markup-brand-symbol/src/htm.ts","hunks":[{"oldStart":37,"oldLines":7,"newStart":37,"newLines":7,"lines":[" (Markup.prototype as unknown as Record<symbol, boolean>